# 🎬 TMDB Movie Data Analysis — Entertainment Industry Project

An end-to-end data analysis project exploring 5,000 TMDB movie records to answer real streaming industry business questions. Data was cleaned and engineered in Python, then visualised in Tableau.

---

## Project Overview

| Detail | Value |
|---|---|
| **Data source** | TMDB (The Movie Database) API |
| **Raw rows** | 5,000 |
| **Clean rows** | 4,682 |
| **Columns (clean)** | 15 |
| **Tools** | Python (stdlib only) · Tableau |

---

## Business Questions

| # | Question | Business Relevance |
|---|---|---|
| Q1 | Does being popular actually mean being good? | Content acquisition & platform strategy |
| Q2 | Which old movies are still pulling audiences today? | Catalog licensing & library acquisition |
| Q3 | Which upcoming 2026–2027 movies are generating the most pre-release buzz? | Release forecasting & marketing spend |
| Q4 | Are audiences rating movies more harshly in recent years? | Quality benchmarking & trend analysis |
| Q5 | Which critically acclaimed movies are flying under the radar? | Recommendation engine & subscriber retention |

