## Engineered Features

| Column | Type | Logic |
|---|---|---|
| `popularity_tier` | String | `Viral` (≥50) · `Very High` (≥20) · `High` (≥10) · `Medium` (≥5) · `Low` (<5) — thresholds derived from data percentiles |
| `rating_quality` | String | `Excellent` (≥8.0) · `Good` (≥7.0) · `Average` (≥6.0) · `Below Average` (≥5.0) · `Poor` (<5.0) · `No Rating` (0 votes) |
| `decade` | String | Derived from `year` — e.g. `1990s`, `2020s` |
| `is_reliable` | Boolean | `votes ≥ 50` — filters noise from low-sample ratings |
| `is_upcoming` | Boolean | `year ≥ 2026` — flags unreleased films for Q3 |
| `is_evergreen` | Boolean | `year < 2010 AND popularity > 20` — still trending decades later |
| `is_hidden_gem` | Boolean | `rating ≥ 8.0 AND votes ≥ 100 AND popularity < median` |
| `quadrant` | String | Q1 scatter quadrant — see below |
| `pop_vs_rating_corr` | Float | Pearson r stored as a constant for Tableau reference |

### Quadrant logic (Q1 scatter plot)

Dividing lines: **median popularity of reliable films** (5.86) × **rating threshold of 7.0**

| Quadrant | Meaning |
|---|---|
| `Viral + Quality` | High popularity AND rating ≥ 7.0 |
| `Viral + Poor` | High popularity AND rating < 7.0 |
| `Hidden Gem` | Low popularity AND rating ≥ 7.0 |
| `Obscure` | Low popularity AND rating < 7.0 |
| `Insufficient Data` | votes < 50 or no rating |

