## Key Findings

### Q1 — Popularity vs Rating

> **Pearson r = 0.0792** (calculated on 3,981 films with votes ≥ 50)

Near-zero correlation. Trending content does **not** reliably deliver audience satisfaction.

| Quadrant | Count |
|---|---|
| Viral + Quality | 1,037 |
| Viral + Poor | 954 |
| Hidden Gem | 718 |
| Obscure | 1,272 |

**Recommendation:** Streaming platforms should decouple their homepage trending algorithm from their content acquisition strategy.

---

### Q2 — Catalog Longevity

**86 pre-2010 films** still have a popularity score above 20 today — competing with recent releases for audience attention decades later. High-rated classics (rating ≥ 8) show the strongest retention.

**Recommendation:** Catalog content from the 1990s–2000s with ratings above 7.5 justifies premium licensing investment for platforms building long-term subscriber retention.

---

### Q3 — Pre-Release Buzz (2026–2027)

**192 unreleased films** are already appearing in TMDB trending data.

| Title | Popularity | Year |
|---|---|---|
| Your Heart Will Be Broken | 1,340.9 | 2026 |
| Avatar: Fire and Ash | 397.8 | 2025 |
| Project Hail Mary | 314.9 | 2026 |
| Scream 7 | 245.2 | 2026 |
| Peaky Blinders: The Immortal Man | 230.4 | 2026 |

**Recommendation:** Pre-release TMDB popularity ≥ 200 signals blockbuster-level anticipation — front-load marketing spend on titles crossing this threshold before any paid campaign launches.

---

### Q4 — Rating Trend 2018–2026

*(Filtered: votes ≥ 50)*

| Year | Avg Rating | Avg Popularity | n |
|---|---|---|---|
| 2018 | 6.86 | 7.44 | 123 |
| 2019 | 6.99 | 7.95 | 137 |
| 2020 | 7.16 | 7.31 | 75 |
| 2021 | 7.00 | 8.38 | 105 |
| 2022 | 7.08 | 7.84 | 128 |
| 2023 | 7.03 | 8.94 | 161 |
| 2024 | 6.74 | 8.13 | 198 |
| 2025 | 6.67 | 15.82 | 316 |
| 2026 | 6.66 | 85.69 | 56 |

Ratings peaked 2020–2022 and have declined since. Average popularity in 2026 is **10× higher** than 2023 — more buzz, lower satisfaction.

**Recommendation:** Platforms should recalibrate toward quality signals over content volume.

---

### Q5 — Hidden Gems

**62 films** with rating ≥ 8.0, votes ≥ 100, and below-median popularity — verified quality content audiences aren't discovering.

Sample titles:

| Title | Year | Rating | Popularity |
|---|---|---|---|
| Paths of Glory | 1957 | 8.25 | 5.79 |
| The Legend of 1900 | 1998 | 8.24 | 5.79 |
| City of God | 2002 | 8.43 | 14.10 |
| Seven Samurai | 1954 | 8.45 | 16.90 |

**Recommendation:** A curated "critically acclaimed but undiscovered" shelf — films rated above 8.0 with below-median visibility — is a low-cost, high-satisfaction strategy for platforms competing against blockbuster-heavy rivals.

